messages:
jordan: Heads-up — big banking POC wants streaming + function-calls to our webhook + strict JSON schema output. They also require IP allowlist and SAML SSO. Can eng help with checklist and a minimal sample for the SDK? Need to answer pricing vs Dedicated vs Hosted.

kai (SE): On it. Quick Qs: will the webhook be inside their VPC? do they need e2e encryption with customer keys? :thinking_face:

jordan: Webhook is on-prem, behind a load balancer with static outbound IPs. They want customer-managed keys (KMS/HSM) and audit logs. Timeline: 2-week POC. Customer is sensitive about data residency.

amanda (AE): Pricing note — if they need stable throughput for heavy streaming and low latency, Dedicated reserved is usually recommended. Can estimate commit after we see sample QPS. Also ask legal about data residency options.

maria (security): For SAML SSO + IP allowlist, Private (VPC) deployment is best. If on-prem webhook needs mutual TLS, we can support mTLS to the webhook. KMS/HSM integration is supported but requires Private or Dedicated with encryption-at-rest keys; I'll DM docs. :lock:

kai (SE): I'll put together a minimal Node streaming + function-calls SDK sample that shows structured output validation and retries. Example for server-sent events style streaming:

```js
// streaming sample (node)
const stream = client.responses.stream({model: 'rwd-stream-v1', input: prompt});
stream.on('delta', chunk => {
  // assemble JSON chunks and validate
});
stream.on('tool_call', call => {
  // call customer webhook
  fetch('https://hook.customer.internal/trigger', {method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(call)});
});
```

kai (SE): For webhook auth, use short-lived signing keys (STS) + JWT in `x-rwd-signature` header. Don't hardcode creds in the POC.

jordan: Nice. Do we have a sample schema validator we can attach? They want the model to return a strict JSON object like "{\"invoice\":{...}}" or fail-safe.

kai (SE): Yes — we recommend a post-stream validation step. We'll include a nyc-schema example and a fallback that triggers `tool_call` to our sanitizer. Quick snippet:

```py
# pseudo
obj = parse_stream(buffer)
if not validate_schema(obj):
  send_tool_call('sanitize', buffer)
```

presales-bot: Runbook: https://internal.redwood/runbooks/presales/streaming-poc (check checklist step 3: firewall, step 6: signing keys)

amanda (AE): Next actions: 1) SE sample by EOD tomorrow, 2) Security to confirm KMS & SAML latency impacts, 3) I'll schedule customer sync for Wed. :calendar:

maria (security): I'll confirm KMS/HSM certs and mutual TLS requirements by EOD. If they insist on air-gapped, escalate to Private on-prem proposal.

jordan: Thanks everyone. If SE can drop sample + short runbook I'll send to the customer and ask for IP allowlist. :thumbsup:
